  "material_source_findings": [
    "Helper enters only for live seat, owned pending player/source on Stack, ACTION or ATTACK, still-insufficient resources, positive exactUID, sourceCardID in the proven Prepare cohort, actualOwner/Controller, matchingKind/SourceZone/fromZone and SourceUniqueID. No arbitrary card or nonpending source is inferred.",
    "First two live queue rows must be exact blocking MZCHOOSE/Pitch_before_banish_cost then blocking CUSTOM. Callback must have own card Prepare namespace, actual positive frame key, proven PC and chosen return variable. Actual GetAwaitFrame stores only locals, so sourceUID/mzID/cost/originalrefs equality plus owned pending source are the applicable identity bindings; no nonexistent frame-owner field is assumed.",
    "All17 exact canonical FaBDTDCostPitchChoices producers and their current generated prompt/callback PC match independently. Frenzy uses reserve0/PC5; other named helper callers use reserve1 and matchingPC5or8. No broader typed-cost policy, dynamic external producer or future regenerated callback is approved.",
    "Mapping uses exactly writer null/Removed survivor predicate and counts ineligible live survivors. It intersects only originally offered absolute own-Hand positional refs with current actual helper eligibility; foreign/relative/unknown/duplicate/malformed refs fail closed. It never broadens the candidate set. Removed offered slots are omitted and cannot alias a surviving successor.",
    "Only selected choice is cloned when its Param differs. The live Hand, source object, original queue choice object, frame locals, callback Param, chosen and global variables/state are not rewritten. Repeat save from same live arrays recomputes same result; reprocessing an already transformed copy declines the originalrefs-equality guard rather than shifting again. A reparsed already compact Hand uses identity mapping/no need for a second shift.",
    "If all originally offered candidates are removed, the nonresolving Hand999999 sentinel has no valid GetZoneObject index; existing Core MZCountChoices tests actual slots and reaches zero-choice policy. This is safe no-alias representation, not a new automatic-success/payment policy; component should exercise it explicitly.",
    "Generated callback writes returned chosen before its PC consumes it; prior savedrefs is diagnostic until a repeated pitch recomputes refs. Leaving frame/CUSTOM data unchanged is therefore correct for current exact continuations. Native original Blue6 answer remains unchanged after remapping.",
    "Existing Lunging, declared reaction, plain-barrier, Rise, Rouse and Flock save-copy paths remain byte-identical and disjoint by named prompt/frame/source. No generic rewrite, no live-splice hook, no CORE/parser/generated edits or new framework."
  ],
